WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:03.740
[voice over] They call those transformed by 
the virus…Freakers.

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:05.000
[Deacon] Jesus.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.320
[radio] What’s wrong?

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.880
[Deacon] Freakers.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:15.460
[voice over] Are you ready to fight?

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:19.939
Hello, my name is David Lee, and I’m the
community manager over at Bend Studios for

00:00:19.939 --> 00:00:21.430
Days Gone.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:24.730
Our team has been developing Days Gone for
over 6 years.

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:30.960
At this point, I’m pretty sure we’re so
excited and enthusiastic for April 26 to come

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.870
because our team has put in so much time,
and there is so much space

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:41.109
solely dedicating to create such a wonderful
and unique experience for the PS4.

00:00:41.109 --> 00:00:44.820
With our latest trailer release with the Sarah-Deacon
wedding, we see that Deacon is struggling

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:50.440
with the fact that his wife was taken away
from him by the pandemic that happened two

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.090
years ago in-game.

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:56.530
So especially with our game, our creative
director John Garvin has crafted a story

00:00:56.530 --> 00:00:58.780
and these characters, you’re gonna want
to play through.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:04.960
We talked about a 30-hour golden path, 6
hours of cinematics, and easily 100 hours

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:06.040
worth of gameplay

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:10.220
so I think anyone who’s interested in a
very narrative-driven story but

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:16.200
they also don’t mind driving around a very unique setting, then Days Gone is for them.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:22.140
In central Oregon, anywhere really Oregon,
you’ll have to drive and in our studio,

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:27.880
they, especially our creative director, is very inspired by shows like The Walking Dead, Sons of Anarchy.

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:31.800
Closer to our studio, they actually know how
to ride motorcycles, so for them, they saw

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:35.420
this as a unique opportunity to bring into our game, which allows

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:39.060
different kinds of gameplay mechanics and different methods to go around.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:43.590
As the game gets more developed, we’ve created
more ways to customise your bike

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:46.729
and really, at this point, I think there are
so many variations out there

00:01:46.729 --> 00:01:50.729
that you really can spend hours customising
your bike and make it even better, so we’re

00:01:50.729 --> 00:01:52.039
really excited about that.

00:01:52.039 --> 00:01:56.640
I think, especially with our bike and wet
weather combat skill system is managed,

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.310
like in most games, in the very beginning,
you’ll struggle a little bit.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:02.950
The game’s going to be hard and nonetheless,
it’ll be hard to go around, but the way

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:04.369
you can allocate your skill points

00:02:04.369 --> 00:02:07.360
and especially the way you can upgrade your
bike, you can give yourself an easier time

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.340
but you’re going to have to make the hard
choice of “alright, am I going to put more

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:12.340
points or time into upgrading my skills?”

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:16.720
or “can I make my life a little easier with
the bike?”, or “can I take some time to

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.040
clear out some of the infestation zones?”

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:21.800
to make it so that I can maybe focus more on my skills, and not have to worry too much about

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:25.050
my second fast travel location.

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:29.900
I think if you want things to be easier in our game, you’ll have to take out those infestation zones

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.000
and take out all that landmarking on the map,
make it so you can fast travel on sea, have

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.760
less encounters with the Freakers.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:40.700
The human threat is just as scary as the Freakers,
because you have ambush camps, people just

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.410
riding by wanting to take you out

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:48.880
because it’s after the pandemic, people who survived
an outbreak – they are not going to be nice,

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:53.240
they’re going to do everything to survive, just like Deacon, so you’ve gotta watch out for them.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:58.160
The dynamic weather system we have in our
game plays an important role with gameplay,

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:00.920
with how you drive your bike, especially with
Freakers.

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:05.620
As it gets dark, during the nighttime – that’s when Freakers start to roam around, get more aggressive.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:10.760
especially when it starts snowing, which kinda hardens the Freakers’ skin, gives them some more health,

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:15.020
and makes them more aggressive, so you always
have to keep aware of the weather on top of

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:16.130
just your normal struggles.

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:21.860
You’re constantly kind of on edge, on your
tippy toes, trying to find out what’s the best scenario.

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:28.030
As we talk about the Swarmers, you can see
any from one to 12, cause the Freakers

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:29.110
they like to stick together,

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:32.970
but then you have hordes, and that can be
anything from 50 to 300, and definitely more

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:34.230
than 300 as well.

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:38.580
But Newts, we have Screamers – we actually
showed off another type of Freaker in our

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:39.980
recent World [Series] trailer,

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:46.380
I cannot divulge any information, but he is
big, bulky, and if you see him, you’d want to run,

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:50.060
unless you feel confident to take him down, but there are more types out there that you can encounter

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:54.730
that you always have that second ear when
you’re playing the game, like okay, do I

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:59.080
feel confident to take him down
or should I just drive away and cut my cost.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:04.080
The Marauders are just humans that are kind
of like Deacon, who pretty much do whatever

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:05.420
it takes to survive.

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:10.150
Two years, people who live past this pandemic
after two years, so you’d imagine they’ll

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:11.680
do anything to survive.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:17.440
Regarding the Rippers, they’re pretty much
crazy people.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:22.700
They…once the pandemic happened, they believed
it was a sign from God that this was a good thing,

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:25.620
so they cut themselves, they burn themselves
to be closer like the Freakers,

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:29.310
and they pretty much worship the Freakers,
so anytime you encounter them,

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:33.539
they’re kind of want you to join them or
they’re going to kill you, and you’ll

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.830
have to kill them, and they’re very aggressive.

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:40.330
We haven’t shown this kind of enemy types
yet, but you’ll see very unique types, especially

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.909
with the Ripper community.

00:04:41.909 --> 00:04:45.509
What’s great about the system in our game
is that Copeland’s – that’s the first

00:04:45.509 --> 00:04:47.379
encampment you encounter,

00:04:47.379 --> 00:04:51.319
we have Maddie there, who’s actually a mechanic,
so he’s going to have the best bike parts.

00:04:51.319 --> 00:04:55.530
But then, in the demo that you’ve had a
chance to play, you actually get to join Tux

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:57.169
Camp at the hot springs,

00:04:57.169 --> 00:05:00.240
and out there, [it] has a good manage[ment]
of weapons,

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:04.040
so if you want better upgrades or better weapons,
you’re going to go to him.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:09.100
We haven’t revealed all the camps yet, but know that each camp kind of specifies a different speciality,

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:13.400
and that you’re going to have to make the
decision of “okay, where am I going to focus

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:17.320
doing side jobs, or turning in stuff?” at
each of these camps.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:23.300
I can say that…you know, our team has been working 
on the game for so hard for the past 6 years,

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:28.700
we’re so excited to get our game Days Gone
into the hands of the PlayStation hardcore

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:30.320
fans and the casual,

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:33.759
and we’re so excited to see our game release
on April 26.

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:37.840
[voice over] Explore the world of Days Gone
at your peril.

